  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong dark editorial system, disciplined cyan/red/yellow semantics, and a clear headline-to-ledger-to-conclusion hierarchy. However, desktop composition leaves excessive empty space above and to the right while forcing awkward headline breaks. Mobile is visibly cramped: the cost-per-success row nearly collides, supporting copy is very small and muted, and the header reduces to an unexplained icon with clipped navigation. Tablet is the most balanced viewport.",
    "fix": "Rebalance the desktop hero into a tighter two-column composition, enforce more intentional headline line lengths, and redesign mobile ledger rows so labels and values never crowd. Increase small-copy size/contrast and give the compact header a clearer identity and navigation affordance.",
